.TH TOGGLY-FEATURE 1 "" "Toggly CLI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
toggly-feature \- List, inspect, and manage features
.SH SYNOPSIS
toggly\-cli feature <command>
.SH DESCRIPTION
List, inspect, and manage features
.SH CREATE
Create a new feature definition\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature create \-\-name <name> \-\-feature\-key <key> [\-\-app <id>] [options]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.TP
.B \-\-name
Feature display name (required)
.TP
.B \-\-feature\-key
Feature key used as the application reference (required)
.TP
.B \-\-description
Feature description
.TP
.B \-\-category
Feature category
.TP
.B \-\-tags
Comma\-separated list of tags
.TP
.B \-\-environment\-filters
JSON object mapping environment names to filter arrays
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature create \-\-app <app\-id> \-\-name "New Feature" \-\-feature\-key new\-feature
.PP
Aliases: create\-feature.
.SH GET
Get a feature by key\&. Requires \-\-app or a context default\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature get [\-\-app <id>] <key> [options]
.PP
Arguments:
.TP
.I key
Feature key
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature get \-\-app <app\-id> payments\-enabled
.SH LIST
List features for an application\&. Requires \-\-app or a context default\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature list [\-\-app <id>] [options]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature list \-\-app <app\-id>
.PP
.B toggly\-cli \-\-json feature list \-\-app <app\-id>
.SH UPDATE
Update an existing feature definition metadata\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature update \-\-feature\-key <key> [\-\-app <id>] [options]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.TP
.B \-\-feature\-key
Feature key to update (required)
.TP
.B \-\-name
Feature display name
.TP
.B \-\-description
Feature description
.TP
.B \-\-category
Feature category
.TP
.B \-\-tags
Comma\-separated list of tags
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature update \-\-app <app\-id> \-\-feature\-key new\-feature \-\-description "Updated"
.PP
Aliases: update\-feature.
.SH UPDATE ENVIRONMENT
Update feature configuration on a specific environment\&. Specify exactly one of \-\-enable, \-\-disable, or \-\-filters\&.
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature update\-environment \-\-feature\-key <key> [\-\-app <id>] [\-\-env <name>] (\-\-enable | \-\-disable | \-\-filters <json>) [options]
.PP
Options:
.TP
.B \-\-app, \-\-application\-id
Application id (or set via 'toggly context set \-\-app')
.TP
.B \-\-environment, \-\-env
Environment name (e\&.g\&., Production, Staging)
.TP
.B \-\-feature\-key
Feature key (required)
.TP
.B \-\-enable
Enable the feature (sets AlwaysOn filter)
.TP
.B \-\-disable
Disable the feature (removes all filters)
.TP
.B \-\-filters
JSON array of filter objects
.PP
Examples:
.PP
.B toggly\-cli feature update\-environment \-\-app <app\-id> \-\-env Production \-\-feature\-key new\-feature \-\-enable
.PP
Aliases: update\-feature\-environment.
